#+TITLE: EPURE AutoCAD profile returns C0000005 on an unchanged drawing quit
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation

** Minimal native control
On pfenny, normal interactive Windows account, AutoCAD.Application.24.1
(AutoCAD 2022), create a fresh COM application, wait for quiescence, inspect
the initial document (DBMOD=0), release the document reference and call Quit.
No ALFE, test Lisp, target drawing, runtime trust or file protocol is used.
Temporarily select the existing unnamed profile or Epure before creation;
restore the original profile in finally. Record native PID, creation ticks,
owner SID, kernel handle and natural exit. Never reuse a foreign instance.

| Profile | Native exit | Forced | Error |
| unnamed, no loaded EPURE modules | 00000000 | false | none |
| Epure, initial unchanged drawing | C0000005 | false | none |

A separate visible-window control posts WM_CLOSE to the exact owned AutoCAD
window under Epure; it also exits C0000005 naturally. The corresponding COM
visible-window trial was rejected as transiently busy and forced to clean up;
it is NOT used as successful closure evidence.

** Scope and evidence
This reproduces outside ALFE. It does not identify which EPURE component is
responsible. Loaded native components include DOSLib24x64.arx,
SNCFOutilsARX64.arx, FLSNCFIG.dll and several SNCF DLLs.
Proprietary EPURE sources/PDBs are unavailable to the project maintainer.
Do not blame the ARX's separately established USERPROFILE startup buffer bug
for this shutdown without matching evidence. No vendor binaries are patched.

CI native jobs17691248610 (!507, 4f10bab7) and17691251293 (!476, efb2377f)
pass EPURE API checks and the exact dirty-drawing discard invariant. BricsCAD
COM passes naturally with exit0 in both MRs; BricsCAD batch also passes in
!476. AutoCAD exits BABE variants or C0000005, without forced cleanup.
The lifecycle JUnit records these as failures. A first-chance AV monitor
attached after the test observed no C0000005 exception in one C0000005-exit
trial; its earlier startup was not monitored, so the exit remains unclassified.

** Required resolution
Identify and correct the EPURE profile shutdown defect, or obtain vendor
confirmation of its intended exit contract with sufficient independent crash
evidence. Do not whitelist C0000005/BABE, kill the process as success, or
disable vendor shutdown callbacks merely to obtain a green pipeline.
Keep both MRs unmerged and native qualification blocking.

** Offline shutdown dump analysis (2026-11-03)
The existing PID1072 termination dump retains the active exception's original
CONTEXT and EXCEPTION_RECORD, despite lacking an ExceptionStream. x64 unwind
metadata reconstructs RtlDispatchException/KiUserExceptionDispatcher and the
original failure: read of address zero at ntdll+9750,
RtlpCoalesceFreeBlocks+300 -> RtlpFreeHeap -> RtlFreeHeap -> _free_base ->
AFX_MODULE_STATE::~AFX_MODULE_STATE+82 during CRT/MFC DLL process detach.
Microsoft PDBs identify the object as _afxOleModuleState and the CString
member being released as m_strUnregisterList (offset 104). The relevant heap
blocks are absent, so the originating overwrite/free remains unattributed.

ProcDump records C0000005 before this diagnostic's natural 012EBABE exit.
Therefore that particular BABE value accompanies a real access violation;
absence of a WER event does not establish a clean exit. This is a private
ALFE2.3.91 diagnostic with candidate plugins, not a final-head MR result or
the independent pure-COM control. SNCFOutilsARX64.arx and DOSLib are already
unloaded; FLSNCFIG pointers found in raw stack memory are not true frames.
Do not assign blame to those modules or the managed SCHMS library without
identifying the earlier writer. No new native test or binary modification
was performed for this analysis.

Detailed evidence, symbol identities and limits:
[[file:../../autolisp-front-end/documentation/epure-autocad-shutdown-offline-analysis.org]].
The ALFE USERPROFILE safeguard is recorded separately in
[[file:../closed/alfe-windows-missing-userprofile.issue]].

** Full first-chance capture (2026-11-03)
Pure COM, no ALFE, Epure profile, DBMOD=0, owned PID36612. ProcDump full
first-chance C0000005 capture is 1444478238 bytes, off-host SHA256 verified:
6fea6f5f93984f2a30f40b365e6171f65fdce56ab16fee752da72c02cd27d91f.
The direct ExceptionStream reproduces ntdll+9750 and the MFC OLE-state
CString destructor path. The adjacent 0x1F0-byte free block has a null Blink
and payload matching _AFX_THREAD_STATE (480 bytes, exact inline class-name
layout). Its m_pModuleState at offset8 overlaps the null Blink: a strong
use-after-free hypothesis. The earlier writer/free caller is still unknown.
This is not proof against a specific proprietary EPURE module.

A page-heap follow-up capture is prepared but could not start: elevated task
creation is denied to PPBN02261. No GlobalFlag change or second CAD launch
occurred. No leftover capture task/CAD/debugger; profile restored, both PF5
runners unpaused. Administrative execution is needed for the next capture.
Detailed receipt, full-memory findings and limits are in the linked report.
Keep the issue open and both MRs unmerged; do not whitelist the exit.

** Administrator-assisted page heap follow-up (2026-11-03)
Global full page heap was enabled by a separate administrator controller;
AutoCAD remained under the existing CAD account. First AV was captured in
memcpy from accore's wide-string initialization before quiescence/Quit,
not in the MFC shutdown path. Source allocation is14 bytes, source+8,
requested copy16: an allocated-buffer over-read into a guard page.
See autocad-pageheap-startup-wide-string-overread.issue for that obstacle.
Capture timeout required cleanup of the exact owned instance, recorded as
Forced=true. The controller restored its exact image option, removed the
capture task, and both runners were reactivated. No shutdown success claim.

A 480-byte protected-allocation filter is prepared to target the suspected
thread-state lifetime defect without being stopped by the unrelated small
allocation. Settings are backed up/restored by existence, type and value.
The limited capture task is registered but not started; administrator READY
and a newly coordinated reservation are still required. No merge.

** 2026-11-06: focused PageHeap confirms the stale-state write
Full first-chance shutdown dump PID8152, SHA256
BF7762B63B60CD43AF1AE3C26CD3061056239F1A0F542511B1E2E41195E8D941,
confirms a released 480-byte _AFX_THREAD_STATE. AfxTermExtensionModule
frees it; AFX_MAINTAIN_STATE2::~AFX_MAINTAIN_STATE2 later writes NULL at
user+8 (mfc140u+137b4c), naturally exiting C0000005 with no forced close.
CLR target token060004e4, a unique observed native precode and independent
IL/native-thunk review strongly identify SNCFEG_Traverses64.dll's
On_kUnloadAppMsg -> CAcExtensionModule.DetachInstance path. Shared-stub
and reconstructed Desktop CLR layout limitations are documented, rather
than treating a creator Module pointer alone as attribution.
See the dated section in the offline analysis report for exact addresses,
free stack, hashes and restoration receipts. All analysis ran off Windows.
IFEO/profile were restored and runners released; no product fix or merge.
This issue remains OPEN pending a source-level lifecycle fix and native
qualification. Do not suppress the crash or remove Detach without its SDK
ownership contract and validation.
